# CORE ERP AUDIT, STABILIZATION, INTEGRATION & PRODUCTION READINESS

You are working on an EXISTING multi-school School ERP Management System.

This is NOT a request to create a new project.

Your primary objective in this phase is to audit, stabilize, complete, integrate, secure, and make the existing ERP production-ready.

DO NOT rebuild the application from scratch.

DO NOT create a second ERP.

DO NOT replace working modules unnecessarily.

DO NOT create duplicate entities, duplicate dashboards, duplicate databases, or duplicate business logic.

Before changing anything, inspect the complete existing codebase, database schema, migrations, API routes, server actions, authentication system, RBAC, components, pages, existing modules, and current implementation status.

==================================================
1. CORE OBJECTIVE
==================================================

Perform a complete CORE ERP AUDIT and then implement/fix everything required for a reliable basic School ERP.

The following core workflow must work correctly from beginning to end:

School
→ Academic Session
→ Class
→ Section
→ Subject
→ Student
→ Parent/Guardian
→ Teacher/Staff
→ Teacher Subject/Class Assignment
→ Attendance
→ Fees
→ Payment
→ Receipt
→ Student Ledger
→ Examination
→ Marks
→ Result
→ Report Card
→ Timetable
→ Homework
→ Parent/Student Portal

The system must support multiple schools with strict school-level data isolation.

Every implemented feature must use real database persistence.

No fake buttons.

No placeholder functionality.

No mock production data.

No hardcoded business records.

No frontend-only security.

